  "abstract": "We keep the proven Fourier Forecaster LN with learnable \u03b3[t] (p=36, H=160, drop=0.05) and only change the loss: a normalized step-weighted MAE that emphasizes late steps by +10% (mean weight=1.0) plus the standard temporal curvature penalty (\u03bb=1e-4). Goal: reduce late-horizon errors without harming early steps.",
  "submitted_tick": 307,
  "no_debugger": false,
  "cpu_only": false,
  "original_submission": {
    "content": "import sys\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\n\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\nfrom models_fourier_ramp import create_network as create_base_network\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36,     # p\n        'hidden_size': 160,  # H\n        'drop': 0.05,\n        'gamma_start': 0.25,\n        'gamma_end': 0.99,\n        'learn_gamma': True\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    # Use the proven Fourier LN + learnable \u03b3 backbone from lineage\n    return create_base_network(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    # predictions/targets: (B, 32, N)\n    err = jnp.abs(predictions - targets)  # (B, 32, N)\n\n    # Step-weighted MAE: late steps up-weighted by +10%, normalized to mean 1.0\n    w = jnp.linspace(1.0, 1.10, 32)                     # shape (32,)\n    w = w / jnp.mean(w)                                 # keep overall scale ~ constant\n    w = w[None, :, None]                                # (1, 32, 1)\n    weighted_mae = jnp.mean(err * w)\n\n    # Temporal curvature penalty (second-difference L1 across time)\n    d2 = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curvature = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2))\n    return weighted_mae + 1e-4 * curvature\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 9e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n",
